## 5. SYSTEM MODULES AND FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

### Module 1: Authentication and User Management

Create a complete authentication system using Supabase Auth.

Required pages:
- Student Registration
- Vendor Registration
- Login
- Forgot Password
- Reset Password
- User Profile

Requirements:
- Secure password authentication.
- Email verification where configured.
- Role-based redirection after login.
- Students are redirected to the student dashboard.
- Vendors are redirected to the vendor dashboard.
- Administrators are redirected to the admin dashboard.
- Prevent unauthorized users from accessing restricted pages.
- Maintain user sessions securely.

### Module 2: Food Listing Management

Allow approved vendors to publish discounted leftover food.

Each food listing must include:

- Food Name
- Food Description
- Food Category
- Food Image
- Original Price (RM)
- Discounted Price (RM)
- Discount Percentage
- Available Quantity
- Vendor Name
- Pickup Location
- Pickup Start Time
- Pickup End Time
- Food Availability Status
- Date Created

Food categories can include:
- Rice and Noodles
- Fast Food
- Snacks
- Bakery
- Beverages
- Desserts
- Other

Automatically calculate the discount percentage based on the original and discounted prices.

Example:

Original Price: RM10.00

Discounted Price: RM5.00

Discount: 50%

Listings must automatically become unavailable after their pickup deadline or when their available quantity reaches zero.

### Module 3: Food Browsing

Create an attractive food marketplace where students can browse available discounted meals.

Required features:
- Food cards with images.
- Food name.
- Vendor name.
- Original price with strikethrough.
- Discounted price.
- Discount percentage.
- Available quantity.
- Pickup time.
- Add to Cart button.
- View Details button.

Provide search and filtering options:
- Search by food name.
- Filter by food category.
- Filter by price range.
- Filter by vendor.
- Sort by lowest price.
- Sort by highest discount.
- Show only available food.

Display a suitable empty state when no food is available.

### Module 4: Shopping Cart and Ordering

Students must be able to select food and place orders.

Shopping cart functionality:
- Add food to cart.
- Increase or decrease quantity.
- Remove food from cart.
- Calculate subtotal.
- Display total discounted price.
- Prevent ordering quantities greater than available stock.

Checkout functionality:
- Display student details.
- Display selected food.
- Display order summary.
- Confirm order.
- Generate a unique order number.
- Generate a unique pickup verification code.

For the initial implementation, support **Pay at Pickup**. Record payment status in the database. Structure the application so that an online payment gateway can be added later.

Do not collect or store credit card information.

Important: Stock deduction and order creation must be handled securely and atomically to prevent overselling when multiple students order the same food simultaneously.

### Module 5: Order Management

Implement the following order statuses:

| Status | Description |
|---|---|
| Pending | Order has been successfully placed and awaits vendor confirmation. |
| Confirmed | Vendor has accepted the order. |
| Ready for Pickup | Food is prepared and ready for collection. |
| Picked Up | Student has collected the food successfully. |
| Cancelled | Order has been cancelled. |
| Expired | Order was not collected before the deadline. |

Students can view:
- Order ID
- Order Date
- Food Ordered
- Quantity
- Total Amount
- Vendor Name
- Pickup Location
- Pickup Time
- Order Status
- Pickup Code

Vendors can:
- View incoming orders.
- Accept orders.
- Update preparation status.
- Mark orders as ready for pickup.
- Verify pickup codes.
- Confirm successful collection.

### Module 6: Pickup Verification

Implement a simple and secure collection verification process.

1. A student places an order.
2. The system generates a unique pickup code.
3. The student displays the code or QR code at the vendor counter.
4. The vendor enters or scans the pickup code.
5. The system verifies that the order belongs to the relevant vendor.
6. Display the associated order and student information needed for verification.
7. The vendor confirms that the food has been collected.
8. The order status changes to Picked Up.
9. The pickup code becomes invalid for future use.

The pickup verification process must not allow an order to be collected more than once.

